  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U1"],
      "pins": ["U1.7"],
      "nets": ["GND", "HOLD_(IO3)"],
      "observed": "On the FCC Peripherals sheet, the Winbond NAND FLASH part U1 (W25N01GVZEIG_TR) has its HOLD_(IO3) pin (pin 7) wired directly to the GND symbol (the same ground node as the EP/pin 4), while WP_(IO2) (pin 6) is driven by a net (NET0160).",
      "expected": "The active-low HOLD# input of the W25N01GV must be held high (tied to 3V3 or pulled up) for the device to be operable; the specification lists this part as the FCC-side 'FLASH Memory' and expects it to function. Sound practice (and the WP# handling on the same part) requires HOLD# not be grounded.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet: U1 W25N01GVZEIG_TR, pin 7 'HOLD_(IO3)' wire runs to the GND symbol below the device"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "'FCC-side FLASH | FCCPeripherals | Winbond W25N01GVZEIG_TR (1 Gb NAND)' ... note 'FLASH Memory'"}
      ],
      "impact": "With HOLD# tied low, the NAND flash is permanently placed in hold state; its serial interface cannot respond, so the FCC cannot read or write the flash memory.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the drawing matches the specification (dual MCU, MIC26903 buck with 6.8k/1.3k divider for ~5 V, LD39200 LDO, INA219 on a 10 mΩ shunt, documented barometer RESET/EOC mix-up), but the W25N01GV flash's active-low HOLD# pin is tied directly to GND, which would leave the flash permanently held and non-functional."
}

